nts: (1) The comment term applies math.radians to a percentage and takes sqrt(2.46*x). The original MI formula uses sin(sqrt(2.46*radians(perCM))), so this matches the reference. The unit conversion still deserves a test at 0%, 50% and 100% comments. (2) The guard at line 104 returns 100.0 when volume or sloc is <= 0. This is a deliberate shortcut, but an empty module scores as perfectly maintainable. (3) mi_parameters (lines 120-142) passes raw.lloc as the length argument, while the comment percentage divides by raw.sloc. The two inputs use different line bases, so check that this is intended. radon/raw.py is where those counts come from, so it needs the most time: how comments, multi-line strings and blank lines are classified, and whether sloc can be 0 when comments exist. radon/visitors.py supplies the complexity total (ComplexityVisitor.from_ast) and the Halstead visitor data, so review how branches, boolean operators and comprehensions are counted. radon/complexity.py only needs a brief check of its ranking helpers, since the score uses just total_complexity. In radon/metrics.py, also verify the mi_rank thresholds and that the clamp is applied after scaling.\"}","structured_output":{"minutes":{"A":22,"B":4,"C":14,"D":20},"primary_file":"A","evidence":"The formula is in radon/metrics.py:98-117 (mi_compute). It computes 171 - 5.2*ln(V) - 0.23*CC - 16.2*ln(SLOC) + 50*sin(sqrt(2.46*radians(comments))), then scales by 100/171 and clamps to [0, 100]. Review points: (1) The comment term applies math.radians to a percentage and takes sqrt(2.46*x). The original MI formula uses sin(sqrt(2.46*radians(perCM))), so this matches the reference. The unit conversion still deserves a test at 0%, 50% and 100% comments. (2) The guard at line 104 returns 100.0 when volume or sloc is <= 0. This is a deliberate shortcut, but an empty module scores as perfectly maintainable. (3) mi_parameters (lines 120-142) passes raw.lloc as the length argument, while the comment percentage divides by raw.sloc. The two inputs use different line bases, so check that this is intended. radon/raw.py is where those counts come from, so it needs the most time: how comments, multi-line strings and blank lines are classified, and whether sloc can be 0 when comments exist. radon/visitors.py supplies the complexity total (ComplexityVisitor.from_ast) and the Halstead visitor data, so review how branches, boolean operators and comprehensions are counted. radon/complexity.py only needs a brief check of its ranking helpers, since the score uses just total_complexity. In radon/metrics.py, also verify the mi_rank thresholds and that the clamp is applied after scaling."},"ttft_ms":2555,"type":"result","duration_ms":13228,"uuid":"4263c1e4-b91c-45f8-ab30-7aca3a2f6271","ttft_stream_ms":1652,"time_to_request_ms":108,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":1,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":62,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":8,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":57,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":134,"process_rss_mib_result":205,"process_anon_mib_result":122,"process_peak_rss_mib":228,"process_cpu_ms_turn":531,"process_wall_ms_turn":13228,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":171,"process_wall_ms_streaming":9631,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_count":195,"main_stream_chunk_count":34,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":171,"wall_ms":9631,"entries":3},"tool":{"cpu_ms":26,"wall_ms":26,"entries":1},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":235,"wall_ms":3428,"entries":3},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":57,"wall_ms":1